!ReelEGL - Reel, drawing through EGL (an example)          0.3
===================================================================

ReelEGL is the Reel video player built a second way: the picture goes
through riscos-mesa's EGL instead of Reel's own sprite plotting. It is
here as a working example of an EGL program (FFmpeg's ffegl library,
ffegl_draw_surface), and to compare the two. Everything else - the
controls, keys, menus, sound - is the same as Reel: see !Reel's !Help.
Both can run at once (they have different icon bar icons: ReelEGL's
reel has a green hub).

How it draws
------------
- In the window, the picture is an EGL "work area surface": a surface
  of fixed size at the top of the window's work area, under which the
  controls are ordinary Wimp icons. Each frame is converted by swscale
  straight into the surface (EGL_KHR_lock_surface) and eglSwapBuffers
  shows it; redraws plot it with eglPlotSurfaceRISCOS.
- Full screen uses EGL's whole-screen surface. With Direct ticked (the
  window menu; the default) frames go straight into screen memory: no
  plot at all, the fastest way, but you may see tearing. Without Direct,
  EGL plots a sprite after waiting for the vertical sync.
  *Set ReelEGL$NoDirect 1 starts with Direct off.

Needs
-----
As Reel. The EGL and OpenGL libraries are built in (from riscos-mesa
20.3.5-7pre12); no modules are needed for them.

